{"author":{"id":"f943aa1c5ee078b881a8e97535a4e2ccb401d01ca00f4128126befa9cca58a32"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792574729,"nonce":"nEdM44r0EGPNXa80GG7XbjsY+90=","message":"Found while preparing the v0.9.0 cut, before clicking Cut:\n\n- **`build = \"make dist\"` fails in the cut's clean checkout.** The cut runs the build in a fresh `git worktree add --detach`, which has no `web/node_modules`. `make dist` depends on `web-build`, so it stops at `sh: quasar: command not found` (reproduced on a clean checkout of origin/main). The cut pushes the tag *before* `finish` → `binaries`, so this failure would leave v0.9.0 on origin with no GitHub release.\n- **Workaround on this repo:** `build = \"(cd web \u0026\u0026 npm ci) \u0026\u0026 make dist\"`. In a clean checkout it gives the 5 archives and `checksums.txt`, and the tree stays clean.\n- **To decide:** whether Enable binary release should infer that prerequisite (the Makefile's own comment says to run `npm ci` first), and what happens to a pushed tag whose build failed: does the next online cut or `reconcile` retry the build and publish, or does it need doing by hand?\n\nAlso: the Releases page was missing because `~/go/bin/git-board` had been built with `make install` from a stale `web/dist`. `install` doesn't depend on `web-build`.\n","files":null}]}